## 4. Operation schema (A1)

`schemas/operation.schema.json` (JSON Schema 2020-12, `$id` .../0.1.0/operation.schema.json) has a
`$defs/operation` envelope and a `$defs/operationType` enum with the 19 types, dispatched with
`if`/`then` to one payload definition per type:

    operation envelope  id, boardId, actorId (UUIDv7), createdAt (ISO-8601), type, payload, inverse
    19 types            createNote/updateNote/deleteNote, createCard/moveCard/resizeCard/deleteCard,
                        createZone/moveZone/resizeZone/deleteZone,
                        createBlock/moveBlock/resizeBlock/updateBlock/deleteBlock,
                        createEdge/deleteEdge, group
    inverse             exactly one object {boardId, type, payload}; boardId must equal the
                        operation boardId (checked by the tests, see section 6)
    payloads            create* store the entity; update* store only changed fields, minimum one;
                        move* store x/y and an optional zoneId parent; resize* carry the P1-01
                        minimum sizes; delete* store the whole object; deleteNote stores note +
                        cards (AD-4); deleteZone stores zone + content policy keep/delete + members
    group               payload.children = ordered full operations (minItems 1, no group child);
                        group-inverse-payload.children = inverse pairs (minItems 1)

The operation schema is exported by `index.mjs` (`SCHEMA_FILES.operation`, `schemaId`,
`schemaPath`, `fixturePath`, `OPERATION_TYPES`). The entity schemas and `board-content` are
unchanged.

## 5. Fixtures (A2)

42 operation fixtures under `fixtures/operation/` in the `{schema, valid, reason, data}` wrapper:
19 valid (one per operation type) and 23 invalid. Every type has a valid and an invalid fixture; the
invalid ones name the violated rule, for example:

    invalid-create-card        card height 79 is below the card minimum 80
    invalid-resize-card        width 175 is below the card minimum 176
    invalid-resize-zone        height 191 is below the zone minimum 192
    invalid-resize-block       table width 287 is below the table minimum 288
    invalid-create-edge        an edge endpoint must be a card; a zone endpoint is invalid
    invalid-update-note        changes may only contain known fields
    invalid-update-block       changes must contain at least one field
    invalid-group-empty        a group needs at least one child
    invalid-group-nested       groups do not nest
    invalid-group-not-reversed the group inverse must list the reversed child inverses
    invalid-inverse-board      the inverse boardId does not match the operation boardId
    invalid-inverse-target     the inverse target id does not match the operation target

All 77 contract fixtures (35 board-content + 42 operation) parse and map to their schema.

## 6. Tests (A3)

37 tests, 37 pass. The operation suite (`test/operations.test.mjs`, shared validator and helpers in
`test/support.mjs`) covers: the operation schema and type enum, index exports, fixture coverage per
type, fixture wrapper and mapping, schema validation of valid fixtures, rejection of invalid
fixtures, exactly one inverse per operation, UUIDv7 ids / ISO timestamps, the documented inverse
type per operation, ordered group children and the reversed child inverses, no nested groups and
minItems 1, updates storing only changed fields with previous values in the inverse, deletes storing
the object and creates inverting to deletes, resize minimum sizes matching the P1-01 entity schemas,
move payloads with position and optional zone parent, and the two model-only invalid cases
(mismatching inverse board, mismatching inverse target).

JSON Schema cannot compare values across fields, so the model rules that need it are checked by the
tests in addition to the schema: inverse board/target equality, exact-one-inverse, group reversal,
no nesting and the update field rules. Invalid fixtures are rejected if they break the schema or one
of these model rules; the two model-only invalid fixtures are schema-valid on purpose.

