## 8. Known limits and open questions

- The inverse of `deleteNote` and `deleteZone` is a `group`, because those deletes remove several
  objects and the contract keeps exactly one inverse per operation. The group inverse contains
  inverse pairs (type + payload, no ids/timestamps); P1-04 (sync) must define how these pairs are
  applied and P1-03 (codegen) how they are typed.
- `updateBlock` can only change `zoneId` in 0.1.0 because block content is not modelled yet; block
  content updates need the block-content contract.
- Cross-field rules (inverse board/target equality, group reversal) are enforced by the test suite,
  not by JSON Schema. A generated runtime validator in P1-03 must repeat them.
- Move/resize operations store the previous position/size only; multi-step undo history is engine
  behaviour (P4-05), not part of this contract.
